          <change when="2022-01-23T11:25:09-05:00" who="https://papyri.info/editor/users/Mike%20Sampson">Vote - AcceptText - Agreed. Theta is oblong in shape elsewhere (e.g., l. 14), and the parallel is good.</change>
          <change when="2022-01-23T07:37:17-05:00" who="https://papyri.info/editor/users/james.cowey">Vote - AcceptText - A section of the horizontal fibres is broken off, which leaves only traces of the two letters following epsilon. The chi had been read and is relatively clear. The little cross like traces just above the broken off section fits nicely with a theta which is rather egg shaped and not rounded at the top. Looks like a good supplement to me. </change>
          <change when="2022-01-23T06:18:18-05:00" who="https://papyri.info/editor/users/gclaytor">Submit - new reading in l. 9, supported by parallels (e.g. https://papyri.info/ddbdp/sb;16;12696). There are no BL corrections for this papyrus.</change>
